Z||000000||TRiAD||05-30-2001||11:22 AM||||What suspension is everyone running?<BR>I'm wanting to lower front and rear, and make the handling as precise as possible. Adjustability is a plus.<BR>Is "the Fiero Store"'s Koni complete kit any good? What springs do you all recommend?<BR>The car will have a V8 in it eventually, I know that will matter. <BR>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Looking for a white '88 GT 5 sp</I></B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-30-2001||11:47 AM||||I have the Fiero Store KYB set-up. I rode in  friends with the KONI's. I don't know if his were adjustable or how he had them adjusted but on Illinois roads it was VERY rough. (KYB's are not adjustable) Mine is pretty stiff with the KYB set-up but not as bad as the stiff KONI set-up.<BR>The Fiero Store kits come with Eibach lowering springs, (1.5" drop. They say 1" but after the suspension "settles" it's closer to 1.5") and Suspension Tech Sway bars (one size larger than stock with poly bushings). I also went with poly bushings all the way around which also stiffened up the suspension too.<BR>I like the way mine is set-up. I would say as a daily driver its a little stiff but not bad considering the roads here are not too good. You can feel all the expansion joints when going down the highway. It handles like it's glued down and corners great.<BR>Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SloPonti||05-31-2001||12:20 AM||||i am running poly bushings on all four corners plus poly sway bushings and poly engine cradle mounts and dogbone! i have intraxx lowering springs! i see you are in morton- i live in peoria-come to peoria and i can give you a ride!! <BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
